  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets in the dead of night.\nEach step echoed on pavement stone,\nAlone, yet never quite alone.\n\nLike ghosts, the people drifted by,\nWith vacant eyes and averted eye.\nTheir faces buried, deep and wide,\nIn worlds where he could not abide.\n\nAmidst the urban, heaving sea,\nA profound solitude set free.\nNo touch, no word, no glance, no sound,\nJust silence in the hallowed ground.\n\n***\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the **giraffe**."
